Of, Steams, CoveringFireOf, FocusOf. 0.34.2: Sky 2026-10-26, the patrol seeing the Enter is no fail: a seen act it reports (rulebook cell.enter.seen; GameEntrySeen.cs). 0.34.1: brief 067, Aster's ruling within Motive's M067-SQ2 (ai.noStall): an advance closes on its operative: a rival advancing on an operative takes a cover only if its walk to him is strictly shorter than the walk from where he stands and it lies inside his effective reach of him or nearer him than he stands (Game.ClosingCover; SelectCover's order, the first that closes), else his stop point of him, else he holds; on that walk he takes no kite step out of a line (Hostile.Closing, as K3's walk to a held car: with the cover rule alone a kite step turned each walk back to cv-029, every 2.2-2.5 s); 0.34.0 left out only the cover he held, so in ra-h3 rival-3 went back and forth between cv-030 and cv-029 every 1.8 s (4:13.9-4:21.1), never nearer the Tech (scenario SQ2-CLOSES). 0.34.0: brief 067 (Sky playing 0.2.122; Motive briefs/067/motive-values.json, Pulse and Vantage briefs/067): (1) no input hangs the engine: a harness bounds every game it makes in Step calls (Game.HarnessStepLimit, Scenarios.StepLimit 60,000; RunawayException) and check and batch watch every play (--timeout, default 300 s): S10 waited for the patrol's sweep to come onto the public door, which the yard sweep never does, and stepped its finished run for ever; (2) the walk split (M067-B1): cell.speed is the cell's (op-speed-cm-s 180), crowd.walk the city's (people-walk-cm-s 140: the summoned partner, reporters and tellers, a witness to a body, the crowd back from shelter, the rounds bake's pace); op-run-speed-cm-s 360, carry-untrained-cm-s 90, mod-running 375; (3) attention.run (M067-B2): a run is seen and suspicious, never an Alert on its own (cell.runAlert retired): a clock-keeping watcher that sees it jumps its clock to the notice mark, then counts it as standing still; run.seen logs the sighting once a run; (4) M067-K3 (fight.unguarded) as Motive amended it (briefs/067/motive-square.md §4): with Vale in the car, the car held and nobody of the cell standing outside it, the rivals walk to the car (rivals.for-car; back to cover once someone stands outside again or the car is free, rivals.back-to-cover); a free car with the cell aboard waits for Go; the cell down fails at once (cell-down), Go needs a standing op aboard (car-no-driver); (5) Pulse: a post's waiting point is its door's post for the check-in marks (people beside; guard 73 marks again from 5:30), the Office's staffed doors face the kerb; (6) the debrief names no sweep gap where the sweep never sees the door (RouteBot ""); fight.safe is not logged when the crew is wiped at the start; the patrol's reroute lines name no place; (7) M067-SQ1 (the hold is entered only on purpose): in the final fight an answer to fire (a rival's step out of a line or to cover, a police body's cover or close) never ends inside fight.hold of the car or on its exit lane, else the body stands; a walk to a post goes round the hold (the rival crew to its spots, police and the response unit to their stands: RouteRoundHold, MoveToFight); car.held.<how> logs the first tick each body holds the car at a stand (blocker, press, advance, answer, post; Hostile.Why, log only); (8) M067-SQ2 (no stall): a rival holding with nobody in his reach for ai.engageLapse advances again (ai.advance) on the nearest operative standing on the street he has cause to fire on, to the cover that shields him from that operative, else to the first point of the walk to him within his stop reach that has the line to him (StopPointSeen: Motive's sketch stopped where it stood, 12 m from the Enforcer and blind to him, and asked again every second); with nowhere to go he holds, silent; (9) the site fact patrolWatchesEntry (suborned-sim facts; Game.PatrolWatchesEntry, SweepSecondsOnEntry), for Waymark's MC-3: false on the yard sweep, true on 0.33.1's forecourt (59 s of 100). 0.33.1: brief 041 (Sky pla